# 🗣️ 3️⃣3️⃣ INTERVIEW COMMUNICATION 🎤

### Question:

**"Why would you use BFS instead of DFS to find the shortest path in an unweighted graph?"**

Strong answer:

> “BFS explores the graph level by level. Therefore, the first time it reaches a node, it has reached that node using the minimum number of edges from the source. DFS does not guarantee this because it can explore a deeper path before discovering a shorter one.”

